laurel 2401: Wi-Fi on the Mi A3 (SM6125 trinket, WCN3990 through the modem), on by default. Values from the downstream trinket.dtsi: modem carve-out pil_modem_mem 0x4b000000+0x7e00000 (topaz checked 0x4ab00000+0x6900000; our modem.mdt loads 0x4b000000..0x52e00000), WLFW MSA wlan_msa_mem 0x53300000 size 0x200000 (qcom,wlan-msa-fixed-region: icnss takes the region size, icnss.c:3767-3791), WLAN SMMU stream 0x80 mask 1 (topaz 0x1a0). New: the WCN3990 supply votes icnss makes (RPM SMD ldoa 8 0.64 V, 16 1.8 V, 17 1.304 V, 23 3.0 V, uv + swen, both sets); a refused vote turns the radio off with one line, the modem still boots. MODEM_POOL_BASE/SIZE: one place, 'pool map owned by area A (docs/laurel_sprout/memory-map.md)', static_asserts: no overlap with the GPU pool (area B 0xC0000000+0x20000000) and below 0xF0000000; the topaz value 0xE0000000 stays until the coordinator sets the final map (it collides with area F's audio pool). modem=1/wifi=1 opt-ins become modem=0/wifi=0 kill switches. Status line: 'LAUREL WIFI: on: modem up, WLFW ready, board id 0x.., MAC .. (modem_b)' at WMI READY (also after an earlier off), or 'LAUREL WIFI: off: <reason>' once at the first failure: firmware partition (2400), apps SMMU, RPM supplies, each TrustZone PAS step (init_image / mem_setup / auth_and_reset with ret/res), carve-out layout, modem crash reason, modem not READY in 60 s, no WLFW in 30 s, WLFW stuck (step) 60 s, no WMI READY 30 s after mission mode; the WLFW timers start again when WLFW restarts. Unchanged topaz values checked against trinket.dtsi: SMEM 0x46000000, TCSR mutex 0x340000 (hwlock 3), APCS 0x0F111000 (SMP2P 435/428 bit 14, GLINK modem bit 12), apps SMMU 0xC600000, CE 0xC800000+0x240000 (polled, no SPI 358-369), RPM msg RAM 0x45F0000, rmtfs on modemst1/modemst2/fsc/fsg.

